/*
  X-Content-Type-Options: nosniff
  X-Frame-Options: DENY
  Referrer-Policy: strict-origin-when-cross-origin

# the faun seal of the deploy lanes: the engine keeps its runtime sqlite
# stores beside the working directory (vault-storage.db, uistore.db, the
# wal and shm sidecars), so a publish lane that mounts the application root
# would ship the whole store over https. The seal is layered — the publish
# dir is the build output only (netlify, vercel and workers mount dist; the
# container serves /app/dist through the api.ts static lane, which refuses
# a database file outright), and even a stray database face inside this
# publish tree answers sealed: never cached at the edge, never indexed,
# never rendered inline.
/*.db
  Cache-Control: no-store, max-age=0
  X-Robots-Tag: noindex, nofollow, noarchive
  Content-Type: application/octet-stream
  Content-Disposition: attachment
/*.db-shm
  Cache-Control: no-store, max-age=0
  X-Robots-Tag: noindex, nofollow, noarchive
  Content-Type: application/octet-stream
  Content-Disposition: attachment
/*.db-wal
  Cache-Control: no-store, max-age=0
  X-Robots-Tag: noindex, nofollow, noarchive
  Content-Type: application/octet-stream
  Content-Disposition: attachment
/*.db-journal
  Cache-Control: no-store, max-age=0
  X-Robots-Tag: noindex, nofollow, noarchive
  Content-Type: application/octet-stream
  Content-Disposition: attachment
